From: CEB-GNRD platform <ceb-gnrd@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] webui: give the date display notice the full content width

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD settings layout]

Keep the date/time display preference notice permanently visible and use
the full row instead of half the desktop content width. Keep its sentence
and Profile Settings link inline with comfortable line spacing, allowing
natural wrapping on narrow screens while keeping the link label together.
Only this informational notice changes; the date/time form is untouched.

--- a/src/views/Settings/DateTime/DateTime.vue
+++ b/src/views/Settings/DateTime/DateTime.vue
@@ -2,14 +2,14 @@
   <b-container fluid="xl">
     <page-title />
     <b-row>
-      <b-col md="8" xl="6">
+      <b-col cols="12">
         <alert variant="info" class="mb-4">
-          <span class="no-underline-link">
+          <p class="mb-0 lh-base no-underline-link">
             {{ $t('pageDateTime.alert.message') }}
-            <b-link to="/profile-settings">
-              {{ $t('pageDateTime.alert.link') }}</b-link
-            >
-          </span>
+            <b-link to="/profile-settings" class="fw-semibold text-nowrap">
+              {{ $t('pageDateTime.alert.link') }}
+            </b-link>
+          </p>
         </alert>
       </b-col>
     </b-row>
